  "briefing": [
    "Larkspur House, Wiltshire. Sunday 18 November 1962, nine o’clock in the morning.",
    "Last night Lionel Thorne — sixty-three, self-made, founder of Thorne Instruments — was found dead at his study desk, less than an hour before the midnight toast at which he meant to ‘clear the decks’ with an announcement.",
    "The storm flooded the only bridge out of the valley. No one came and no one went. Six people were in the house with him.",
    "Constable Pike, out of his depth and soaked to the knees, has sealed the study and asked you to look into it before the county men can get through. His notes are in the file. Everyone, he says, has something to hide.",
    "Find out who killed Lionel Thorne, how it was done and why — and be ready to prove it."
  ],
